Apple today updated its TestFlight app for iOS, iPadOS, macOS, and visionOS to version 4.4.0, adding support for features introduced in the latest software updates and products.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/01/TestFlight-Banner.jpg" alt="" width="1200" height="630" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-986098" /><br/>
TestFlight for iPhone supports landscape orientation ahead of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>'s October launch, though the option is available on all iPhones. TestFlight can now be resized when using iPhone Mirroring on a Mac running macOS 27 with an iPhone running <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Apple says the update also includes unspecified stability improvements and bug fixes. <br/>
